            <profile id="1f10-88e1-c272-9ffd" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, shield, bow and thrusting spear. May have light armour (+2 pts), heavy armour (+3 pts) and may be Drilled (+1 pt). May also have either half-barding (+4 pts) or cloth barding (+4 pts). Open Order. With heavy armour they are Eastern Shock Cavalry; otherwise subject to Eastern Shock Cavalry rule 1. May only be chosen if an Army General has been chosen as well. 0-1 unit. (Armies of Chivalry p.53)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="4ea9-03a6-2346-47e2" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
