  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ce70-50d4-337f-1097" name="Ottoman Turks (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>THE OTTOMAN TURKS c.1280-1517 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.52-53). Mehterhane: the Mehterhane characters must be placed in the same unit as the Army General; the unit is immune to panic and each Mehterhane model adds 1" to the General's Leadership radius (max +3"). Camels: place kneeling or standing camel models in base contact with the rear of the unit; formed units with Camels cause fear in enemy cavalry; if the unit charges or flees the camels are removed and it no longer causes fear. Vassals documented only: 0-2 Byzantine Regular Pronoiarios (Last Byzantines list), 0-2 Balkan Cavalry (Serbians from Hungary and/or Wallachian Calarasi), 0-1 Voynuks (Regular &amp; Militia infantry from Moldavia/Wallachia), 0-2 Vassal Archers (Archers, Hungary list).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[The Ottoman Turks - Ghazi Ottomans]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Turkoman &amp; Akincis Cavalry: at least 50%
  Volunteers: up to 15%
  Vassals: up to 100%
  Ghazi Ottomans c.1280-1361. Characters up to 25%, Turkoman Cavalry at least 50%, Volunteers up to 15% (no handguns), Ottoman Cavalry 0-2 Sipahi units (may not take heavy armour), Vassals 0-2 units of Mountain Tribesmen. Ghazi special rule: any unit may be upgraded to Ghazis for +1 pt per model; Ghazis may re-roll their first failed Panic test.
[The Ottoman Turks - Conquest Ottomans]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ottoman Cavalry: at least 25%
  Turkoman &amp; Akincis Cavalry: up to 15%
  Volunteers: up to 25%
  Janissaries: up to 33%
  Vassals: up to 50%
  Artillery: up to 10%
  Conquest Ottomans 1361-1517. Characters up to 25%, Ottoman Cavalry at least 25% (at least one unit of Sipahis), Akincis up to 15% (10% minimum if no Infantry including Vassals are taken), Volunteers up to 25% (10% minimum if any Infantry including Vassals are taken), Janissaries up to 33%, Vassals up to 50%, Artillery up to 10%. Special rule: all Ottoman artillery may be equipped with Master Gunners at +20 pts per cannon.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
